  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Public transit is divisive. It's a messy \nsubject worldwide where politics, sociology,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and economics all clash. But nowhere does it draw more controversy and deliver worse results  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10400,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than in the United States. This is the richest  nation on Earth. Yet, driving is far more common  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than public transport, and ridership here is low relative to any other developed country.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's not an accident. In the decades after World War II, the US deliberately reshaped itself into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a car-centric nation. Dense transit-dependent urban centers gave way to sprawling suburbs of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single family homes on quarter-acre lots. The American Dream sold families on a big house,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37520,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a yard, the latest appliances, and your own car in the driveway. It was a cultural identity that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43280,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had long existed, but after the war was reshaped into an ideological construct and marketing tool.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US government used the American Dream to reintegrate veterans, fuel consumerism, motivate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the population, and showcase capitalism over  Soviet-style communism. Home and car ownership  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were elevated not just as domestic status symbols, but promoted as global proof that only American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capitalism could deliver mass prosperity and equal opportunity. While war torn Europe nationalized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "key services like health care, education, and transit, America in the same period subsidized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suburban mortgages, rewarded mass production homes, and funded the surrounding infrastructure.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With a steady stream of buyers, private developers made fortunes building wherever land was cheap.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Walkability and transit didn't matter. Meanwhile, car makers, oil companies, and tire manufacturers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lobbied for highways and actively dismantled street cars to ensure that cars would become the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "primary mode of transport for future generations of Americans. While Europe and Asia invested in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "public transit and compact urban development, the US funneled hundreds of billions of dollars into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interstate highways, enabling suburban homeowners to commute to urban jobs by car. All of these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measures not only fueled sprawl, but also diverted investment away from urban housing and public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit. Today, the United States stands alone as the only country where suburban car-dependent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121760,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single family housing is the norm. Yet, cities like New York City, Chicago, Washington DC, San  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Francisco, and Boston all boast the highest public transit ridersihp in the country despite this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "generational prioritization of cars. While public transit has been underinvested through history,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not accurate to say that there's been no investment. US public transit agencies serve fewer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "riders than their international counterparts, yet cost more money than anywhere else with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annual operating budgets that exceed billions of dollars. But whether it's rampant crime and poor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hygiene or just basic on-time performance and fare collection, public transit in America consistently  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158640,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ranks amongst the worst in the developed world in nearly every metric. Every year they set a global  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "record for how much money they lose. Adjust for currency, normalize into percentages, and the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169440,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "answer is the same. No one offers less, spends as much money, and still somehow loses more on public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174960,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit than America. This isn't a post-COVID issue or one-year anomaly. These are the average annual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181040,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operating margins for each agency over the past 6 to 15 years. Transit advocates regularly trumpet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that public transit is an essential service, not a business, and that measuring profit is useless.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They point to valid double standards like how US roads themselves to this day are not fully  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funded by drivers and their losses are covered by taxpayers. But guess what? Even the transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203200,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "systems in Europe and Asia that Americans idolize, the Taipei subway, the Tokyo subway, the Madrid  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209280,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Metro, or the Paris RE all chase profit. These agencies not only boast the best on-time rates  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and highest ridership in the world, but also operate like for-profit businesses. They publish  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220320,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annual reports, share progress, outline clear goals, track revenue, and explain their financial  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226560,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "performance with the same diligence as a publicly traded corporation. The hard truth that Reddit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "idealists struggle to face is that profit is the best measure of effectiveness and efficiency.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When money is the primary input and constraint, no metric matters more than the bottom line. Profit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a forcing function and feedback mechanism. It tells you when something's broken and pushes you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to either work smarter or harder. Even NGOs and charities evaluate themselves on how much money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they bring in, their impact relative to their spend, and how much money is left to keep going.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257840,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the world's leading transit systems optimize for profit just as much as performance. It's not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Europe and Asia have perfected public transit, even though they've invested more.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268160,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reality is that every agency is constantly overcoming the same obstacles of labor shortages,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273680,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worker strikes, service complaints, bureaucracy, aging infrastructure, and funding challenges.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Money is scarce everywhere. It's not like the Tokyo, Paris, and Berlin metros get blank checks.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most agencies are still able to rake in consistent operating profits, showing that it is possible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to operate public transit without losing money. For those that are not profitable, they actively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "control their losses and they find ways to do more with less. The Taipei Metro and Seoul Metro,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for instance, have experienced declining ridership and profits since COVID. In response, they've cut  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306560,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "service, frozen hiring, and suspended raises. The profitable Berlin BVG, Hong Kong MTR, Tokyo Metro,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314240,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Taiwan HSR invest their surplus by upgrading systems, hiring more staff, and giving  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bonuses to their existing workers. In short, these agencies all operate within the boundaries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325840,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of profit and loss, deficit and surplus, revenue and expenses accordingly, no different from how a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regular for-profit business behaves in the private sector. Contrast that with the US, where transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agencies make no attempt to be independent. They burn through billions, ask for more, burn through  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that, and still cry about being underfunded. Even as service and rider experience decline,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they serve fewer writers and smaller populations, but still employ the same, if not more workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the leading Asian and European systems. Instead of managing finances, they double down,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hiring more people and raising wages year after year, further deepening their losses. Unless  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers in Japan, Taiwan, Italy, or even France are naturally more productive than Americans,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no justification for higher costs and worse results. Underinvestment can explain delays,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it can't explain this level of chronic \nmismanagement and inefficiency. Only in America,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where capitalism supposedly rewards efficiency and value, has public transit become this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dysfunctional machine that serves only to enrich unions and workers, fraud and corruption get a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slap on the wrist. A manager had sex with his subordinate multiple times on the clock and both  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396080,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weren't fired. A station agent pocketed fares for over a decade and retired with a full pension. A  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customer service rep claimed to work a 100-hour work weeks to steal a quarter of a million. A  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foreman made nearly half a million while being at home during shifts he claimed to be working  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yet faced no punishment. A janitor took home $270,000 but was found napping in the storage  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "area as a ploy to milk overtime. and 10 years later, he's still there. This isn't a case of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few bad apples. These incidents span different agencies and cities. It's not mismanagement or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incompetence. It's corruption and embezzlement. And it's systemic in American public transit.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434320,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ironically, this doesn't happen in the EU or Asia. Not even the French with their 35-hour work weeks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440480,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aggressive worker protections, and militant unions engage in this kind of behavior. Corruption has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been institutionalized at nearly every major transit agency in the US across decades. This is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452160,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the real reason why politicians prefer to repave intersections or add lanes to busy highways even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though they know it won't solve congestion. Road work has predictable costs, a clear scope of work,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "concrete turnaround, and nets visible even if temporary results. In contrast, money given to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "public transit vanishes into a black hole only to be met with complaints that it still wasn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473760,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough. What many Americans fail to understand is public transit requires good governance with the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479520,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrong leaders, broken incentives, complacency, and systemic corruption. More money just leads to more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "waste. Yet, the prevailing attitude nationwide is apathy. You get the sheltered Americans who claim  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that public transit is totally acceptable. They've personally never had a bad experience their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whole lives. Then there are the activists who dismiss economic realities and live in fantasy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shouting that transit should be free and that billion-dollar losses don't matter. Next are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the defeatists who assert that inefficient and ineffective transit is just a natural part of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "city life. Then there are the apologists who invent all sorts of geographical or technical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reasons as to why public transit is uniquely difficult in America, as if the engineers in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Europe and Asia build their systems on flat land and perfect weather. And finally, there's the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524480,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "older generations who are so vested in suburban life and home appreciation that they don't think  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "urban public transit matters at all. In this episode, we dive into transit systems around the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world to expose the uniquely rotten economics of American public transit, where unions drain public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539680,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds, stifle innovation, and cut backroom deals with politicians to protect their own interests.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does the future hold in business? Ask nine experts and you'll get 10 answers. Tune in to any  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "news program and you'll get pundits talking about equities, interest rates, and inflation. One week  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they'll talk about how it's going up and then say it's going down in the next. Could someone please  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "invent a crystal ball? Until then, over 42,000 businesses have future-proofed their business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567120,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with NetSuite by Oracle, the number one AI Cloud ERP, bringing accounting, finance, inventory, and HR  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into one fluid platform. With one unified business management suite, there's one source of truth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giving you the visibility and control you need to make quick decisions. With real-time insights and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585120,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forecasting, you're peering into the future with actionable data. When you're closing the books  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in days, not weeks, you're spending less time looking backwards and more time on what's next.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Modern MBA is small at the moment, but as soon as we scale, we will need and use NetSuite. Today,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599360,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're stitching things manually, and it's gotten harder to assess our business health.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to track production costs to run payroll compliant with multiple states and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to evaluate profit and loss by team and project. As a corporation, we pay tax throughout the year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's a nightmare jumping from system to system just to get one answer. These  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are capabilities that only NetSuite provides and it's a platform we intend to take every advantage  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of. Whether your company is earning millions or even hundreds of millions, NetSuite helps you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "respond to immediate challenges and seize your biggest opportunities. Speaking of opportunity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630640,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "download the CFO's Guide to AI and Machine Learning at netsuite.com/MODERNMBA. The guide  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637520,
    "dDurationMs": 10800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is free to you at netsuite.com/MODERNMBA. netsuite.com/MODERNMBA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we covered earlier, public transit in the US is an anomaly because of how the country was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shaped after World War II. Beyond the American Dream and suburban housing boom, it was the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "auto industry who pushed for roads over public transit. Manufacturers like Ford and General  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Motors alongside their partners like Standard Oil and Firestone Tires all saw this historic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opportunity to turn generations of Americans into lifetime customers. They didn't just lobby  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673600,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the 1956 Interstate Highway Act. They also tore out the pre-existing widely used street  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "car networks across cities, forcing millions to become car owners with no other remaining  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alternatives for commuting. Decades later, the US maintains this political commitment to free market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "principles in individual liberty with most goods and services provided and shaped by the private  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sector rather than the government. We can see this at a macro level as America overall across federal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700640,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and state consistently spends substantially less of its GDP on its citizens when compared to other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developed countries. But it's not necessarily about the overall percentage but what it gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allocated towards. After all the mandatory programs like social security and Medicare,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the single greatest category that gets the most funding is national defense. Throughout history,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US military-industrial complex has been the most well-funded category and highest national  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "priority, garnering hundreds of billions \nof dollars every year. America invests more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollars into warfare than everything else that builds a country, like education, agriculture,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy, and transportation. This isn't a new development. It's been like this for generations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741520,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under both Democrat and Republican rule. After defense, transportation gets a fraction of what's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left. Even during the suburban American Dream and highway construction of the 1960s and 70s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752880,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transportation never made up more than 8% of federal spending. But this isn't unusual. France,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Germany, and Spain invest even less of their GDP into transportation infrastructure. The difference  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763840,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that for the US, highways, unsurprisingly, have received the overwhelming majority of investment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769520,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ahead of public transit and airports. From the 40s to 70s, every penny went directly to highways. As  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the interstate highway system neared completion in the 1980s, federal funding naturally declined  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781520,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from roughly 80% of transportation to about 70% in later decades. While public transit was clearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787840,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deprioritized, it wasn't abandoned. Since the early 2000s, federal investment in public transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793840,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has steadily increased from just a few percentage points to nearly 30% today. Even under both Trump  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "administrations, funding has remained largely intact. Even though highways still get the lion's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "share, there's clearly been a change in attitude towards public transit over the decades. It's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "objectively not as fast or as big as it should be. But we're still talking about tens of billions of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollars every year distributed directly into the pockets of transit agencies across the nation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819760,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the $226 billion invested in the past decade, money is hardly a valid excuse for the state of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American public transit today. Of the billions that each agency has received directly from this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pool, other developed countries have spent the same amount to build a brand new metro system or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "highspeed rail. Anyone who's run any business knows that it's not about how much you spend,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's how you spend it. European and Asian countries do have that advantage of speed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and efficiency and that they can move faster with centralized planning, design, and construction.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Public transit overseas is a national priority and their governments can cut through all the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "red tape overnight. Whereas American agencies must navigate state and local politics themselves just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get projects on paper. But while this explains why it's so slow to break ground, it still doesn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explain where exactly those billions of dollars have disappeared to. The go-to excuse across the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nation is that all the money gets eaten up by deferred maintenance. Every agency insists that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875760,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keeping these 70 to 100year-old systems running after decades of neglect is simply that expensive.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maintenance, they say, drains the budget and leaves nothing for upgrades. So any modernization  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requires billions in additional capital funding. But even if all these agencies directed their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds to capital upgrades or new projects, they'd still be bleeding money and spiraling into ever  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greater deficits. The real cost drivers are the absurdly inflated labor costs around the country  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901680,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that come from union lock-in, chronic overtime abuse, artificial overstaffing, inflated salaries,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bloated pensions, and contractual work rules that serve no purpose except to extract more pay while  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the clock. Don't take our word for it. Morrison and Forester, one of the most prestigious American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "law firms, arrived at the same conclusions in writing. The New York MTA had hired them in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mid 2019 to audit its perpetual runaway labor costs. The unions ended up stonewalling the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lawyers during their two-month investigation, and the report was quickly swept aside once COVID  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "took over headlines. Still, labor is the largest operating cost for every public transit system in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940160,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world. Regardless of whether their operators are privatized, state-owned, or municipally run,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's singularly more expensive than fuel, parts, maintenance, and rent. Even in Asia,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the large populations and collectivist culture have kept salaries low for generations,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956320,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "labor remains the single highest cost for the leading transit systems in Hong Kong, South Korea,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962080,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Taiwan, and Singapore. Only a handful of agencies have labor costs well below 50% of their operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967760,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "budget. Among them are Boston's MBTA, London's TfL, Tokyo Metro, and Japan's privatized JR rail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies. These are outliers who have achieved their dramatically lower labor costs through  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979280,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outsourcing or culture, as we'll analyze later. But for the most part, the majority of the world's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit systems are run in-house. Public transit is inherently labor intensive, even more so  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than manufacturing. They're open systems, unlike factories, and they deal with so many different  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "variables that the best solution is often still manual. Buses and trains have to be driven.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Staff must be at stations and on standby at all hours to address issues. And facilities can only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be manually inspected, cleaned, and maintained. Even if we set aside the issues surrounding unions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and funding, automation will always be tricky to implement given the sheer number of edge cases and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high stakes of safely moving thousands of humans around in a small fleet of vehicles. The other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020880,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reason for universal high labor cost is that public transit work is hard and unattractive.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Working as a bus driver, station attendant, subway cleaner, or rail mechanic is not easy. These are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not jobs that most people would leap to do, and their skills are not easily transferable to other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1036480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sectors. Unless you relocate, there's only ever going to be one, maybe two systems that you could  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever work at within a single city. When we look at average wages, we can see that every transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operator in the world pays a premium to attract and retain talent. If we looked at absolute  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amounts by currency, the US would lead every time by the strength of the dollar alone. The only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fair comparison is to normalize for currency and cost of living by measuring compensation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061760,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a percentage above the local average. In Asia, transit workers make on average 52% more compared  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a full-time worker in the same city. This is total compensation, which includes benefits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pensions and are real dollar costs for every agency, even if it's not captured in an immediate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paycheck. And in Europe, the premium for transit workers across the continent is 38%. Higher pay is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084320,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just the cost of business in public transit. But the US surpasses both continents with the highest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paid transit workers in the world, averaging total compensation that's 114% higher than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095120,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "full-time salaried workers in the same cities. New Jersey and New York pay the best with compensation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "premiums well above the national average. The SF MUN, which ranks seventh in the country with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106480,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ridership below Chicago and Washington DC, pays their workers as much as a mid-level software  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineer. There's another way to visualize just how much better paid American transit workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are compared to their overseas counterparts - wage multiple. This metric shows how many times  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a transit worker's pay exceeds the local median income. When we rank the 23 agencies in our data  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "set by wage multiple, American agencies dominate. 8 out of the top 10 are in the US with workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that earn two to three times the local median income. Now, a better paid workforce can be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "justifiable if they're more productive, effective, and able to render higher quality or larger scale  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144480,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "services. But if we rerank all 23 agencies in our data set by ridership, we find there's virtually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no relationship between how well workers get paid to how many riders they're able to service. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything, it's the inverse. The agencies that move the most people consistently operate with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lower wage multiples, while US agencies serve the fewest riders yet pay the highest relative  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to local incomes. Next, we can measure the labor productivity of each agency by the number of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "writers that each employee serves. But when we divide the number of riders by the size of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforce, we find that all of the US agencies aren't just overpaid, they're overstaffed. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "serve the fewest number of riders per employee while paying the highest wage multiples in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world. Despite their labor advantages, the Asian agencies are ironically the most lean, as they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "serve the most number of passengers for the fewest number of employees. There's nothing wrong with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paying above market wages when it's the global standard. But if you're paying the highest wages,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "double Europe, and four times that of Asia while losing millions or billions annually, something  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206400,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to change. To reduce labor cost, you can lay off staff or lower salaries. If you can't do those  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things, then at the bare minimum, you can contain the cost by freezing hiring and raises. This isn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217520,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a sociological debate or some twisted Wall Street formula. It's just basic math. Instead, American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224320,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit agencies around the country all make the worst possible choice. They increase their labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229280,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs on every front, expanding headcount by 2 to 5% and issuing 2 to 7% raises year after year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235840,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for over a decade. As a result, labor costs have spiraled so far that no amount of federal funding,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ridership growth, or fair increase could ever keep up. In contrast, every profitable European  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247680,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Asian transit agency reinvests its surplus into either headcount or wages, never both. Labor costs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stay contained because they commit to holding one constant while raising the other. It's ironic that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1259200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "socialist Europeans and collectivist Asians are better capitalists than the Americans themselves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it comes to public transit. When you're deep in the red, paying top dollar salaries and still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "handing out raises and/or adding headcount every year, that's beyond bad business. Asia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a region is often ridiculed as simply riding the cattails of globalization. But when it comes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279840,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to public transit, it's leading, not copying. Whether it's South Korea, Taiwan, China, or Japan,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286480,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these countries all boast world-class systems with incredible networks, reliability, punctuality,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1293120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speed, cleanliness, safety, and comfort that are simply unimaginable in the West. These countries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all have weaker economies, currencies, buying power, and poorer citizens. They don't have the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consumerism and foreign investment that the United States uniquely enjoys where they can just print  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309120,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cash or rack up debt to fund new projects. With less cash at hand and a higher margin of error,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the leading transit systems in Asia defy logic in both operations and business performance. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shanghai and Beijing subways enjoy the highest ridership in the world, but without public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325680,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "financials, our next best option is the Tokyo Metro. It's one of the world's most consistently  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profitable agencies with an average annual operating margin of 15% in the past 8 years,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even during COVID. They're a for-profit \npartially privatized transit operator that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "receives no operating subsidies from the Japanese government. Self-sufficiency is not a goal, it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a requirement. If they need funds for day-to-day operations, they must generate that revenue and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352080,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profit themselves. Ultimately, sustainable public transit isn't rocket science. You control labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs on one end and maximize revenue on the other. Tokyo Metro's profits come from their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exceptionally low labor costs, which represent less than a quarter of their annual operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367600,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expenses. This means that for every $1,000 that the agency spends, only $240 goes to workers, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the remainder is split between utilities, energy, equipment, and parts. They've barely grown since  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380320,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2017, with the average annual workforce growth at just 0.2% per year. And while workers still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387040,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make 25% more than the median full-time employee in Tokyo, they've received virtually no raises for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392880,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the past 8 years. Median worker compensation has increased just 0.6% per year during that period.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1400000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, transit workers real wages have effectively declined and consistently lagged  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404960,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behind inflation and cost of living. This is a product of culture and economy as much as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1410160,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efficiency. The Japanese live to work rather than work to live as the society upholds job dedication  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416240,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "above personal health. Japan's economic stagnation since the 1990s is well documented. Wages have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stagnated not just for transit workers, but across the private and public sector as well. Meanwhile,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the nail that sticks out gets hammered down. The local emphasis on conformity, social harmony,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and civic duty discourages dissent, no matter how disgruntled workers may feel. Tokyo Metro  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1438400,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers are unionized, but these cultural norms still prevail. Under Japan's enterprise unionism,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444320,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the focus is on cooperation over confrontation. Strikes are symbolic, disputes are handled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1450080,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "privately, and negotiations are collaborative. Since the Japanese value employment over wages,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they have a vested interest in making sure the company, or in this case, the transit operator,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can survive long term. As a result, the Tokyo Metro unions have historically focused their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "efforts on preventing layoffs rather than issuing aggressive wage demands. At the same time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Tokyo Metro is exceptional at generating and collecting revenue. Japan's high trust  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "law-abiding culture combined with a closed fare system results in one of the lowest fare evasion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rates in the world. This also helps keep labor down, safety up, and efficiency high as they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't need ticket inspectors like most systems depend on in the West. Tokyo Metro makes 90% of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its money from tickets and the remaining 10% in advertising and real estate. They follow the rail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus property strategy where stations are not just stops where people can get on and get off but also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1502480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hubs that they can shop and eat at. And since the infrastructure already exists, the agency extracts  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508160,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "further revenue from these existing assets by renting out these valuable hoot traffic spots.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1514080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Tokyo Metro is profitable and gets no operating subsidies, they still need help to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518720,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "afford the big projects like line modernization, \nnetwork expansion, station remodeling, and fleet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upgrades. Despite their strong track record, and global reputation, Tokyo Metro gets no slack.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530640,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They must demonstrate financial viability, cost effectiveness, and return on investment on every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proposed capital project to secure any external funding. The agency isn't just required to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantify the projected benefits and justify their needs. It must also prove that it can cover the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long-term maintenance and operating costs without subsidies. But even after approval, the national  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "government only funds at most 1/3 of construction costs. Tokyo Metro as an agency must come up with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the remaining 2/3 on their own, whether that's through profits, bonds, or bank loans. As the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563120,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "majority backer, this is financial accountability by design. If a project overruns or underperforms,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's money the agency won't ever get back and consequences that they must live with.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1574560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These same business principles govern Japan's other transit agencies which operate at an even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1579440,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greater scale. There's JR West and JR East who handle not only urban rail like Tokyo Metro but  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1585360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also longer distance inner city rail, inter-regional bullet trains and buses. Both have been profitable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the past 10 years. Like Tokyo Metro, they get zero operating subsidies and are required  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596320,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be financially sustainable. As fully privatized for-profit corporations, JR West and JR East have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1603040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taken the rail plus property business model to the highest level. They build, manage, and rent office  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buildings, shopping malls, apartments, and even hotels around their stations on top of the usual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1614080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in-station retail. They even operate their own travel agencies and contactless smart card systems  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to drive further dollars from banking and tourism. Growing passenger flow through stations is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1624240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ultimately the biggest driver of land appreciation and rental income. As a result, public transit has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become more like a loss leader that drives cash flow but little profits. If we look at just the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit business, we can see that on average both agencies just barely break even, meaning all the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639920,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profits come from the other businesses. Still, even with higher margin ventures, both agencies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are still constantly adjusting to financial realities. It's a simple calculus. If riders  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651200,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and revenue are down, then costs must come down. JR East serves the most riders out of the three,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1656560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but has seen declining ridership and fare revenue since co. So, they've downsized by shrinking their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1662240,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit workforce by an average of 5% every year. JR East isn't laying off workers. They've just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1668160,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opted not to backfill the people who've retired to maintain their profit margins. For the transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1672720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers that have stayed, they're actually paid a greater premium than their Tokyo Metro peers, but  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677280,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their rates have remained just as stagnant. Total worker compensation has grown at just 1.2% per  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683600,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year for the past 8. While JR West fare revenue has rebounded to pre-COVID levels far more quickly,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the same variable, different inputs. \nThe riders are back, revenue has recovered,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694320,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so costs can remain flat. As a result, JR West hasn't cut staff as aggressively as its eastern  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1700480,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "counterpart, but worker compensation hasn't grown at all over the past decade. JR East, JR West,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1706800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Tokyo Metro aren't capitalists squeezing workers or state-backed entities walking around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with blank checks. They've all succeeded by operating rationally within business constraints  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and adjusting to the economic and cultural realities of their country. The Taipei Metro  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722720,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is another example of the property plus rail model in action, but under a more Americanized culture.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With roughly 2 million in annual ridership, it's smaller in scale compared to the Japanese systems,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1733840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not any less sustainable. Looking \nat historical annual operating margin,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738480,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Taipei Metro trails the Tokyo Metro, but is on par with JR West and JR East. With a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more individualistic culture, stronger economy, and better work life balance relative to Japan,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "labor costs for the Taipei Metro are 58% of annual operating expenses, which is closer to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the benchmark of transit agencies in the West. Taipei Metro workers are unionized and relative  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1761200,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Japan are far more outspoken given their ties to Taiwan's political parties. But the unions have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1767200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "focused far more on worker protection than wages, potentially because of just how significantly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1771840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well- paid the transit workers are, especially for the public sector. Taipei Metro workers are paid  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1777280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at significantly greater premiums above the local standard, especially when compared to Japan's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit agencies. Taipei Metro has historically reinvested its minimal profits into its existing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1788320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforce. Workers have received standard cost of living increases of 2.3% for the past decade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1794640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The agency has accounted for these greater costs by controlling headcount. The workforce has grown  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799680,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less than 1% on average year-over-year over the same period. Same calculus. If riders and revenue  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are up, then you can spend surplus to grow either wages or headcount. While Taipei Metro has turned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1811840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some stations into shopping malls and retail spaces, passenger fair still accounts for over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816400,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "80% of annual revenue. Because it's municipally owned and operated, the agency has never needed to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aggressively pursue commercial opportunities and rental income like privatized operators such as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1827840,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "JR West and JR East. But ridership has declined since COVID and the agency has been unable to shake  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1834160,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losses with a fare-centric business. Taipei Metro receives no operating subsidies despite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its ownership model. Breaking even is expected and losses are unacceptable. Now with four  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1844800,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consecutive years of operating deficits, Taiwan is urgently exploring ways to close the gap. Whether  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1850560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's eliminating discounts, raising fares, or expanding on rental income, all options are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now on the table. The Taipei Metro relies on the national government to fund capital projects. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1861120,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the Tokyo Metro, still undergo scrutiny for every proposal. They must prove a self-liquidity  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1866800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ratio of one or higher, meaning that the project will generate enough income to cover its future  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1872000,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operating costs. If a project's SLR scores below a one, it gets rejected. Even the largest, most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1878480,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prestigious transit agency in Taiwan must still prove business ROI for funding. Hong Kong's MTR,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1885760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a partially privatized rail and bus operator, is the world's most profitable transit agency. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1891360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MTR does not receive any operating subsidies or outside funding for capital projects. Ironically,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1897120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their capitalist excellence is fueled more by their colonial upbringing and communist governance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1902000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than the free market. Like it is in China, all the land in Hong Kong is owned by the state.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1907200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can only own the structure built on top of the land like the building, house, apartment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1912000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or office. You lease the land from the government for decades at a time. It's a huge contrast from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1917120,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US, the West, Japan, and Taiwan where when you buy a property, you own the land and structure. In  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1923360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "countries where private land ownership is a thing, most of the value is in the land. Buying houses in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1928400,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Bay Area, Manhattan, Tokyo, or Taipei is expensive, not because of how nice they are,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1934240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because of how scarce the land is in these desirable areas. This is why appreciation is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1939520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much lower in arrangements where you buy the structure, but not the land, like a condo or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1944320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "co-op. In Hong Kong, what began as a mechanism for colonial rule under the British in the 1800s has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1950320,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been maintained by the Chinese Communist Party as a part of present-day Hong Kong. Ownership aside,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "land here is infamously scarce. Hong Kong ranks as the world's most expensive city in price per  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1961760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "square meter, ahead of even Zurich and New York City. With all the land in the hands of the state,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1966800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the government holds tremendous power. They can relocate citizens and reclaim land anytime to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1971840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make way for public transit. As the MTR's majority owner, the Hong Kong government  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1976560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grants the agency direct access to land at preferential prices that no private developer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1981840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could ever obtain. Life revolves around the MTR as car ownership in Hong Kong is among  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1986960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the lowest in the developed world. When a new MTR station is built, it doesn't just improve  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1991840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "access to another part of the city. It instead injects an invaluable supply of housing, retail,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1996720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and commercial space that simply did not exist before. The MTR also gets rights for the adjacent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2001920,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lots. So they also design the surrounding shopping malls, offices, hotels, highrises, parks, garages,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2008720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the roads that connect everything together. They construct parts of the site  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2012560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves and sell the remaining to developers at a premium. The MTR in effect is more than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2017760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a transit agency. It's the city's most powerful developer, landlord, and urban planner who profits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2023360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directly from the land value they unlock. However, like Taipei, fares still contribute 80% of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2029360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MTR's annual revenue. The cash infusions, profit sharing, and rents from real estate only enable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2034960,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the MTR to fund capital projects on their own. They're not high enough to offset labor costs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2040160,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are the agency's greatest, coming in at over 50% of annual operating expense. Even with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2046320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry-leading margins and a guaranteed cash flow engine, the Hong Kong MTR exercises fiscal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2051680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "restraint and discipline. Land rights are not treated like a license to overspend. profits have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2056800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been reinvested into the workforce as the average MTR worker has enjoyed a median annual raise of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2062080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6% every year for the past 9 years despite the fact that there's no officially recognized union  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2067600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or collective bargaining laws in Hong Kong. Meanwhile, headcount has remained virtually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2072400,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flat with annual increases of less than 1% over the same period. It's the same calculus, increase  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2078640,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hiring or wages, but never both. Singapore has two main transit agencies, SBS and SMRT,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2086240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but only the former has financials. SPS Transit is a majority privatized bus and rail operator  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2092000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a unique model. Their primary customer isn't the public, but the government. The state owns  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2097360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the buses, depots, trains, and stations, and outsources the day-to-day to SBS under multi-year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2103520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "licenses. Compensation depends on performance and payment scales to how well the company can meet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "established service and quality benchmarks. In practice, SPS functions less like a transit agency  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2114640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more like a transit staffing company. They've been able to squeeze profit with an average annual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2119360,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operating margin of 3.5% since 2017, but it's come at the expense of workers. Labor is their greatest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2126160,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cost at 51% of their annual operating expenses. With strict contracts, razor thin margins,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2132480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no hard assets, and a purely transactional relationship with the government, SPS only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2137520,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survives by aggressively controlling labor. They pay the lowest premiums of any transit operator in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2142960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world. Headcount has grown on average less than 1% per year for the past eight. And what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2148400,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little profits existed are reinvested into the workforce with a median annual raise of 2.7% per  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2154640,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year for almost a decade. Singapore caps foreign staff at 35% of the transit workforce for national  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2161200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "security reasons. So with low pay, physically demanding jobs, and limited local interest,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2166400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raises are effectively SPS's only retention tool. But this is Singapore, a one-party state that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2172080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rules with an iron fist, holds strict control over the media, and aggressively suppresses  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2176640,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dissent. SPS's longevity can also be attributed to this political environment. Since the 1960s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2183040,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Singapore has systematically weakened unions with \nlaws that force all worker grievances into state  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2188640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arbitration, impose bureaucratic barriers that make organizing impossible, and punish anyone who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2194000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deviates. In the past 40 years, there have only ever been two transit strikes, and the bus drivers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2199360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "involved were arrested and deported. Asia is home to the world's most profitable transit agencies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2204720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we've covered only the ones with high ridership and audited public financials. There is something  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2209440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that each agency does that's worth learning from, and then other aspects that would be impossible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2213920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to replicate in the West. The property plus rail model would never fly in America because private  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2219040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "land ownership is integral and no government could bypass NIMBYism. The success of both private and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2224800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "public transit agencies in Asia shows that profit has everything to do with business discipline  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2229760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than ownership. With above market wages and constrained hiring across their board,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2234640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their bottom lines are not based on cheap labor, but simply controlled labor cost as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2239040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a whole. Despite their record performance, no agency is free to spend indiscriminately.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2244800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Operating losses are heavily scrutinized and external funding always comes with contingencies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2250240,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oversight and proof of ROI. We can see the same calculus in Europe. Transport for London is the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2256800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continent's largest transit operator by measure of riership and scope covering all the rail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2261440,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "networks from the underground subway to the above ground surface rail on top of buses, major roads,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2267040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and fairies. As a state-owned enterprise, TFL has been unprofitable for much of its lifetime,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2273280,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "averaging annual operating margins of - 35% since 2017. For decades, it survived on a 700 million  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2280960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pound annual operating subsidy. That changed in 2018 when Mayor Boris Johnson's government caught  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2286960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all operating subsidies, contending that after billions in rail modernization, TfL should be able  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2292480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to stand on its own. This made the agency the only transit operator in Europe to receive no operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2298160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidies from the government. Without this safety net, the agency scrambled to grow revenue and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2303120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cut costs. They increased fairs and congestion pricing, tacked on extra fees for non-electric  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2308640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vehicles, sold more advertising space, and even lifted a page from the Hong Kong MTR and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2314000,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "partnering with private developers to turn surplus land into rentable mixed-use areas. On the cost  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2319920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "side, they consolidated management, cut staff, and have kept wage increases minimal. The results  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2325360,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been stark. Median worker compensation has fallen 1% per year for the past 9 years. It's the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2331840,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lowest in all of Europe. The workforce has also shrunk at almost the same pace. TfL is the only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2337680,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leading transit operator in Europe whose staff has decreased every year since 2017. While unpopular,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2344400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the decision to throw the transit agency into the deep end has delivered progress. COVID is really  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2349840,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only reason TfL is unprofitable. Fare revenue, the main cash flow for any transit agency, has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2356080,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only recently returned to pre-pandemic levels. But non-fare revenue, so all the property development,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2361840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "advertising, congestion pricing, has not just doubled in four years. It's grown from 9% to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2367120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nearly 30% of annual revenue. Operating losses have substantially shrunk year-over-year to record  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2372720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lows, and the agency is closer to self-sufficiency than ever. These are simply the fruits of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2377840,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combining basic business and urgency. Since 2020, the UK government has resumed its operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2383680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidies to keep the agency afloat. But those cash infusions are separately accounted for. Yet,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2389120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the issue that remains is the quality of service, reliability, and on-time performance on the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2394160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underground, overground, and Elizabeth line have all declined to levels worse than before COVID  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2399520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and before these cost cutting measures were put in place. The buses have been bearing the brunt  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2403840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of it. Much of this has to do with the staffing structure. Labor accounts for just 27% of TfL's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2409600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annual operating expenses, some of the lowest in the world and on par with the Japanese privatized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2414800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operators. While the core subway and rail are operated in house, the buses are contracted  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2420400,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out to private third parties who get paid by performance like SBS in Singapore. Naturally,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2425760,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "job cuts and stagnant pay have not sat well with TfL's unionized workers. Over the past four years,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2432240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they've staged increasingly larger strikes for better pay and working conditions. The agency  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2437120,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has conceded to their demands, agreeing to raise salaries by 5 to 11% for rail workers. Ultimately,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2443440,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "TfL's push for day-to-day financial independence is a net positive. Being forced to identify and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2449120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find solutions to problems within constraints is healthy. Where can you grow revenue to offset the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2454400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inevitable surge in labor costs without just hiking up fares? How do you improve the rail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2459040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "performance without simply committing more bodies \nto the problem? Without challenges like these,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2463680,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "innovation doesn't happen. RATP is the transit agency in Paris. It's state-owned and operated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2470720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and runs the bus and rail for the city and greater metro. RATP leads the continent in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2475840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profitability with an annual average operating margin of 6% in the past 12 years. This profit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2481600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is derived from government subsidies rather than conventional passenger fare revenue. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2486000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not a blank check or handout. Instead, RATP follows a unique structure where the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2490800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agency is still forced to operate as if it's an independent for-profit company that bears all the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2495840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consequences in the event of a loss. Despite facilitating almost as many riders as TFL,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2501440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "RAP doesn't pocket fares. But if they did, it would never be enough to offset the labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2506400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs even before the pandemic when ridership was high. Instead, all the revenue comes from IDFM,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2512160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the regional transit authority, which is governed by the national government, regional council,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2517200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "city, and surrounding counties. These members all pull together payroll tax contributions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2522480,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the fair revenue to fund the IDFM. The IDFM then pays RATP a predetermined lump sum every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2528960,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year based on the operator's own forecast, which only covers operating costs and capital projects.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2534880,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This annual fee is locked in for four years at a time and every cycle involves tense negotiation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2541040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Naturally, RATP will always ask for more money and IDFM will push back asking for justification  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2547280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or inserting contingencies. The only way RATP can turn a profit under this arrangement is through  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2553120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "performance bonuses. If they hit all their targets in reliability, punctuality, customer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2558480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "satisfaction, and cleanliness, then they can earn a full 100 million euro bonus. miss these targets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2563920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they lose the same amount. In a country with 35-hour work weeks and militant unions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2569280,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this convoluted structure manufactures scarcity. IDFM keeps RAP just alive enough to function,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2575760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forcing it to innovate, maximize resources, and prove their fiscal responsibility before they can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2581200,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ask for more. Because the annual rate is locked in, RAP can't overspend and rack up deficits using  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2587520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money they don't have and won't get. They're forced to find ways to hit their performance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2591680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "targets without simply throwing more bodies at the problem. Because getting funding is such a slow,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2596800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exhausting bureaucratic process, RATP is incentivized to turn a profit to break away  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2601920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from its overbearing parent. Profits not only provide a buffer against shocks, but also give  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2607200,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "RATP the freedom to invest in its own priorities without approval. Consistent and greater profits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2612960,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grants RAP stronger leverage during negotiations for bigger future annual fees. Labor is RP's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2620080,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greatest cost at 53% of annual operating expense. Surpluses have gone mostly to headcount growth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2626960,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "averaging 3% a year over the past decade. Wages though have barely budged with annual increases of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2633280,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less than 1% for the past 12 years. And to prevent labor costs from snowballing, worker compensation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2639360,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has remained fairly stagnant with a median annual raise of less than 1% per year for the past 12.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2645840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This stagnation reflects a wider trend of austerity within France's public sector,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2650400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where wages have been frozen for nearly a decade as the national deficit balloons. The French have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2655680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blown past the fiscal rules of the European Union for decades, borrowing over 100% of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2660800,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their GDP every year to fund their exceptionally generous welfare programs. Every attempt to raise  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2666720,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the retirement age sparks mass protests. This climate is why RATP's unions focus their efforts  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2672640,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on preserving pensions, benefits, and jobs by opposing automation and outsourcing. In Spain,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2678560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Madrid Metro follows a contract plus subsidy model similar to Paris, but at a smaller scale.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2683840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It locks in its costs, operating hours, and performance standards with the regional government  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2688320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in advance, and they're only consistently profitable because of operating subsidies from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2692640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the state. After deducting the fair revenue, the regional government covers its remaining operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2697520,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs and ensures that the agency always breaks even. If the agency wants more money, they have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2702960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to negotiate that upfront and accept higher service obligations in return. So even though  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2707760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the operating subsidy makes up a significant portion of revenue, it's still fundamentally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2712160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "performance-based. If the Madrid Metro exceeds the predefined targets on punctuality, reliability,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2717920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cleanliness, and rider satisfaction, they earn a bonus. And if they miss targets,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2722080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the government pays them less. Their profit comes from these bonuses and any cost savings. If the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2727360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agency is able to deliver on its performance obligations for less than it's budgeted, it can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2732080,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pocket the excess. Like in Paris with the RATP, Madrid Metro can invest profit however it wants  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2738320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and can leverage its track record for more funding in future contracts. Because Spain isn't bound by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2743760,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "austerity measures like France, the average Madrid metro worker has fared better with median annual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2749040,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raises of 3.1% since 2017. But to keep labor costs in check, the annual average headcount has grown  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2756080,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just 0.4% in the same period. As generous as they are with compensation, Madrid Metro shows the same  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2762320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pattern as we've discussed elsewhere. More staff or higher pay, but never both. In Milan, Italy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2768320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ATM follows almost the same script. Contracts with the city government define annual operating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2773680,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs, scope of service, and performance standards years in advance. Like RATP in the Madrid metro,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2779920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ATM can't just bill the city for expenses in the middle of the year. And whatever agreed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2784320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upon operating costs that don't get covered by the fares get covered by the government in full.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2788960,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This model has enabled ATM to break even with an average annual operating margin of 0.3% in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2795040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the past 7 years. Italy's economy resembles Japan's in terms of stagnation, and that's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2800240,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflected in ATM worker compensation. Raises have been non-existent, in fact, for the past 8 years,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2806240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which mirrors the overall wage stagnation in the country. ATM's workforce has only grown on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2811360,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "average 0.9% every year over the past decade. With virtually flat wages and headcount, labor costs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2818320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remain firmly in control. Unions, even with high membership, are limited to brief one-day strikes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2824320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for essential staff, transit workers are required by law to announce their strikes weeks  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2829200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in advance, and they can't stage them during rush hours, so transit never fully shuts down. It's the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2834640,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same model in Berlin, Germany, with the rail and bus transit operator BVG. Missing targets carries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2840320,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real financial consequences. Last year, the city cut BVG subsidies by 9 million for failing to meet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2846720,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their established reliability benchmarks. Even so, BVG has averaged an annual operating margin of 4%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2853520,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the past eight years. The workforce has grown on average 3.5% every year in the past decade,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2860000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but wages have barely moved with a median annual increase of just 0.9%. This is partly due to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2866160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Germany's long-standing austerity measures where cities like Berlin retain low fiscal ceilings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2871280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strict budgets, and can't freely increase spending to cover wage hikes. German unions like Japan's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2877120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "favor a cooperative dialogue centric approach where strikes are only ever symbolic and they all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2882720,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know that job security and benefits are far more realistic demands to make than wage increases.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2888240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Prague shows how the contract plus subsidy model plays out in a worker-friendly market. Alongside  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2893440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Poland, the Czech Republic boasts the EU's lowest unemployment. Here, employers chase workers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2898720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the other way around, and that pushes wages up as companies fight with each other to attract  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2903120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hold on to their talent. As a result, Prague metro workers have enjoyed a median annual raise  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2908400,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 6% in the past 13 years, the highest in Europe. The country's conservative immigration policies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2914880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prevent foreign workers from filling this labor shortage, and it only strengthens the bargaining  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2919360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power of domestic workers. They've only ever gone on strike twice since 2008, both times blocking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2925120,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "layoffs, outsourcing, wage cuts, and benefit reductions. So, the AY's above market raises  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2931120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aren't the result of some unique cultural generosity. It's simply what they need to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2935200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do to keep their workforce happy. Yet, the Prague Metro hasn't allowed this dynamic to drive labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2940320,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs out of control. They pay above local wage levels, issue generous annual raises, but hire  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2946240,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very slowly. Headcount has barely grown with an average of 0.4% per year over the past decade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2952640,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet another example of how even with profits, operators must choose more salaries or more staff.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2958640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The evidence is clear. Whether they're property plus rail or contract plus subsidy, every leading  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2963680,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transit operator in the world runs with the same basic principles. Performance must match spend,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2969440,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "budgets are fixed, costs must be controlled, and ROI must be proven every year. Even in the labor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2975360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "progressive countries like France, Italy, Spain, and the Czech Republic. Only in America do transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2981520,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operators get to treat budgets like suggestions, collect endless handouts with no oversight,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2986240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rack up taxpayer losses to the tunes of hundreds of millions of dollars, and face no consequences  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2991280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with bailouts year after year. In a country dominated by cars, these agencies have grown their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2996560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforces and raised salaries every year to the point that no ridership growth, federal funding,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3001600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or fair hikes could ever offset. When we rank the US leading transit agencies by their ridership,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3007120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all operate in deep blue cities. All \nthe local and state politicians that oversee,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3012000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "govern, and fund these transit agencies have been Democratic for decades. And since at a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3016720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "macro level, funding of urban mass transit has substantially grown over the same period. It's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3021680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not that Republicans are car makers. It's just a lack of common sense and accountability that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3026640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rest of the world has already figured out. The New York Metropolitan Transportation Authority is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3032000,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the biggest and highest profile agency in the US and serves the most riders in the nation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3037760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's split between three separate divisions. New York City Transit, which operates the subways and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3042720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buses, the Long Island Railroad, and Bridges and Tunnels. Because the latter were all built nearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3048080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "100 years ago, and have collected tolls every day since, they're the agency's only profitable,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3053040,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "labor efficient, and fiscally responsible \ndivision. For the others, labor is nearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3057840,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "60% of their annual operating expenses. Both NYC Transit and LIRR bleed billions of dollars every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3064960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year. While in Europe, the subsidies are tied to contracts, performance targets, and oversight,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3070000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no such accountability in New York. The MTA is like a trust fund kid. There's no mandate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3075600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requirement, or even expectation to break even. Every year, it blows past its own forecasted  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3081120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "budget, and the state of New York picks up the tab, no matter how deep the deficit. To paper  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3085840,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the MTA's deficits, the state passes the cost onto New Yorkers, small businesses, motorists,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3091680,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and corporations in the form of tax hikes, surcharges, and fees. In essence, MTA's losses drive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3098160,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York City's record cost of living. If this was Berlin, Paris, Taipei, or Tokyo, management would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3104160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been fired, subsidies would have been adjusted down, and future funds would have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3107920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been withheld until a formal recovery plan was submitted to the government. But instead of being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3112560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forced to improve revenue, cut costs, and achieve greater efficiencies, bailouts have become the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3117680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "default, not the exception for the New York MTA. Like the Wall Street and Detroit rescues after  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3122880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 2008 recession, executives and unions get saved while taxpayers are left holding the bag.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3128400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When there is no consequence for incompetence and failure, it only encourages further recklessness.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3133440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's exactly what the MTA has done. Without any hard limits and an infinite safety net, they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3138880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just keep spending and the state and city just digs around for cash. If not from Uncle Sam, then  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3143760,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from someone else. In this light, underinvestment doesn't even qualify as an excuse. Labor is the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3149840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "greatest annual operating expense at nearly 60%. MTA workers work slow and inefficiently to milk  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3155600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their pay as their raises are based on seniority. Bonuses are awarded regardless of performance,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3160880,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and retirees get to cash out inflated pensions. For 23 years straight, MTA employees have averaged  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3167600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an astounding 6.5% annual raise, a rate that's higher than Hong Kong's famously profitable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3173520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MTR and nearly double that of billion tech companies. Instead of trading off between higher  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3179600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pay and more staff like every other operator in the world, the MTA doesn't even pretend to try.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3185040,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their workforce has grown 6% per year for the past 10 years, twice the rate of every other transit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3191040,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agency in the world. How is any of this possible? The answer is unions. The unions are so powerful,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3198240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "connected, and confrontational that they make the French look like pacifists. The unions that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3203040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "represent New York transit workers routinely push for above inflation wage increases and bonuses  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3208400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without any consideration to the state, city, or public. They're so entrenched in New York City  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3213440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "politics that no candidate can win without their endorsement. In return for votes, politicians  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3219200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quietly pledge to keep funneling public money to the transit agency, to never challenge the status  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3224320,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quo, and to guarantee future bailouts. Even Zohran Mamdami, the Democrat socialist running for mayor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3230480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has built his campaign on the endorsements of these unions. His headline stance is to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3235280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make the buses free, and the unions love it because he's promising them even more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3239360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taxpayer dollars. Despite hiring a thousand more workers a year every year for the past decade,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3245040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the MTA still blows billions of dollars in overtime and somehow can't get the job done.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3250320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Overtime has become a machine for personal gain, earning workers a time and a half their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3255040,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regular pay. Because it's rare for any business to generate enough revenue to cover 150% labor costs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3261440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overtime is tightly restricted in all industries, sectors, and organizations, public or private.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3266560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at the New York MTA and other US transit agencies, it's abused. Thanks to the unions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3271920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these workers don't just chase overtime for the pay bump, but also to pad their pensions. At the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3276960,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MTA, seniority, not merit, determines who gets first choice of overtime shifts. Since pensions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3283120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are based on the average pay of an employes's final three years, many veterans deliberately  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3288240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pile on massive unnecessary overtime in the run-up to retirement to inflate their benefits.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3293680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are MTA workers now collecting $200,000 a year in pensions. Pensions are designed to provide  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3299680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retirement security not meant to be a lucrative windfall. And yet decades of this wage engineering  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3304640,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has turned every worker into an ever-increasing lifetime costs that climbs until the day they die.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3310720,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make matters worse, union contracts are loaded with clauses that masquerade as staff protections,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3316240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but really only exist for workers to be able to extract higher pay while on the clock.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3321200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While transit workers across Europe and Asia are trained to perform multiple tasks for efficiency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3326720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American unions lock transit work into rigid classifications. Every worker is limited to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3332000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a narrowly defined set of tasks and trades, regardless of complexity and availability. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3337600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an electrician finds a loose bolt, they have to call in a track maintainer to tighten it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3341920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if that person's not on site, then all work stops until they arrive. This all leads to lost  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3346880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "productivity and double overtime. Work that could have been done in seconds by anyone can easily  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3351840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn into hours of idling and labor costs snowball while productivity shrinks. When you combine the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3357440,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overtime potential, seniority based compensation, guaranteed bailouts, no performance contingencies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3363520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and absence of oversight, New York transit workers are fundamentally and economically incentivized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3369200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do nothing more than the bare minimum as standing around pays better than finishing the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3374080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "job quickly. This is just the tip of the iceberg. Conductors get paid double for driving a train to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3379600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Mets game, even if it's within their normal 9 to 5. Any track work done at night or on weekends  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3385040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "automatically pays overtime or double time, even if it's been scheduled in advance. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3389680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers purposely avoid daytime shifts just to maximize their pay. Engineers earn double if they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3395040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operate both an electric and a diesel train in the same shift, despite no real difference in skill.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3400240,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maintenance crews get paid 8 hours of work every time they move a single engine in the shop. Even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3404960,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though the task itself only takes 1 hour, the MTA was required to provide free cell phones to train  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3410560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drivers. It wasn't even allowed to call them. So for 8 years, these taxpayer funded phones  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3415520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were just personal devices. These are some of the absurd clauses buried in the labor contracts that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3420880,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make cost efficiency impossible. Each division, department, and manager has the tools to fix this.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3426960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could coordinate in advance so that every trade arrives on time, batch jobs so workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3431600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can move on to backup tasks in the same area, or restructure crews to include multiple trades so  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3436560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that no one is just waiting around. But the apple rots from the top. This culture of complacency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3442320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "abuse, and waste has been so ingrained that even the MTA's own leaders lack the urgency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3447440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incentives, or even integrity to try and change it for the better. Rather than having the department  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3452400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaders self audit, the agency dumps that responsibility onto the MTA Inspector General,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3458080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a completely separate office that can investigate waste, fraud, abuse, and operational efficiencies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3463120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pass on those recommendations. But it has no power to act. The MTA also can't fire workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3469280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without just cause, which means that building a strong enough case to terminate an employee can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3473840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drag on for months or even years, which gives the unions time to shield offenders. Few workers get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3479280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "caught, and when they are, the unions meddle in the hearings for so long that most walk  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3483600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away scot-free. If you thought the labor clauses were absurd, wait until you hear these. In 2024,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3489280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a station agent was caught directing tourists to pay him cash instead of buying their subway  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3493600,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tickets on the designated machine. The worker had been employed by the MTA since 2006. Before the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3499760,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hearing could take place, the worker filed for retirement, which automatically closed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3503440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the investigation and shielded him from any discipline. He walked away with a full pension,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3508400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the years and amounts stolen from riders and agency remain unknown. Three electricians and a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3513920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "repairman pulled their swipe cards so the first to arrive and the last to leave would clock in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3518400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and out for everyone else. One electrician retired before the hearing, and the others  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3523040,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "received suspensions. All of these workers had been with the MTA since 1999. Cleaners pretended  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3529360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to work shifts and racked up hundreds of thousands of dollars in overtime when they were all actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3534000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just chilling at home. None of these cleaners or their supervisors were fired. A dispatcher  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3538720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was caught routinely leaving shifts early and not clocking out in order to inflate overtime  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3543280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pay. He had been employed since 1996. He retired before the hearing could take place. A maintenance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3549440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supervisor would schedule overnight shifts at a work site with one of his subordinates. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3553600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were filmed five different times leaving the job site together in a shared personal vehicle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3558160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to have sex while on the clock. The supervisor was demoted and the subordinate was suspended.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3563920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A back office computer worker spent three years double dipping as an adjunct university professor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3569200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during her MTA shifts and even used her agency emails to run her classes. All she got was a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3575040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "30-day suspension. A machinist pretended to be repairing subway cars when he was really at the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3580080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "airport fixing planes for an airline. He collected paychecks from both companies for 4 years and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3585200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retired before the hearing could take place. A real inspector disabled the GPS device on his  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3590320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MTA truck more than a 100 times in an 8-month period and was found sleeping at home while on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3595360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the clock. He retired with a full pension before the hearing took place. These are just cases from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3600720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the past 2 years. The true scope of wage theft in all of these examples is unknown as allegations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3606320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are limited to the time frame in which there is evidence. These sweeping union protections  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3611120,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all but guarantee that most abuse gets buried. If having sex with a subordinate while on the clock,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3616960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "secretly working another job during your shift, faking time sheets for overtime, and stealing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3622000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the company doesn't get you fired or cost you your pension, then what will? What message does  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3627200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this send to their co-workers and colleagues? When incompetence and unethical behavior go unpunished,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3632240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's demoralizing for anyone that's trying to make a difference. Ultimately, the unions only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3637200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have one objective, which is to funnel money from the agency into their members pockets. And they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3641920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "achieve it not just through these absurd labor clauses, ironclad protections, and aggressive wage  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3646720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "demands, but also by keeping corruption buried beyond these few isolated cases. They collude to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3652320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obstruct the MTA at every turn, encouraging members of one union to use swipe cards,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3657360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another union to keep using manual punch cards, and a third to keep writing on paper logs so  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3662400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the agency will never be able to modernize, centralize, and audit payroll under one single  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3667840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electronic system. And even today, they're still out there demanding more money, better benefits,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3673280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and less work for their members. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3757760,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " New York City gets all the attention, but it's the same deal at every other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3764400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leading American public transit agency. If we were to go through every transit agency, their unions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3770160,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their labor contract clauses, this episode would be another hour long. Ultimately,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3774720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the same conundrum. Budgets are treated like suggestions. Public funds flow in without  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3779600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any oversight. Accountability or contingencies. Workers are incentivized to do only the bare  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3784880,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minimum for pay and seniority. Overtime abuse is rampant. And unions operate unchecked in power  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3790800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and demands. Enforcement, ethics, and efficiency are not embedded within any agency, but instead  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3796640,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dumped onto a toothless inspector general who can only investigate a few cases a year. The LA Metro,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3802800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where fair revenue has been declining long since before CO, somehow has the money to blow on median  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3808320,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annual raises of 6.1% for its staff over the past 8 years. The Chicago CTA at a median annual rate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3816000,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 3.5% per year for the past 23 years. With more and more employees netting six-figure pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3822560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from 5 figure bases through overtime, labor costs have only spiraled out of control,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3827120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the AY's operating losses have nearly tripled in that same time frame from hundreds of millions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3832240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to now billions. The CTA is now promising its local politicians that they'll hire more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3837520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employees to cut down on this overtime, seemingly unaware that that will only deepen the hole. It's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3843120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same case with New Jersey Transit, which has given their staff 3.4% raises per year for the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3848720,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "past nine years, even though fair revenue has declined since 2016. Without revenue growth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3854480,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losses have only magnified. The most egregious is the DC Metro, where workers have enjoyed annual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3860080,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raises of 7% every year for the past 23 years, outpacing even the Hong Kong MTR. Their workforce  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3867520,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has grown 2% annually over the same period with no attempt to even trade off between salaries and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3873360,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "headcount. It's no surprise that DC Metro loses the most out of any transit agency in the world.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3879680,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Philadelphia SEPTA, San Francisco's MUNI, and the Bay Area BART are all in the same boat. Unchecked  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3885280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spending on raises and staffing has driven all these agencies into deeper losses, and there's no  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3890080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "revenue growth or ridership growth to turn things around. The point isn't that transit workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3895040,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should never get raises, but when they're already earning a minimum 50% premium over local wages,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3900640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "labor costs are already elevated. When transit agencies can pile up bills without oversight,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3906000,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get bailed out over and over again with no consequences, and face no pressure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3909920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be fiscally responsible, the unions get to exploit this gap every time, funneling most of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3915040,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the taxpayer dollars into workers' pockets without delivering any cost-justifiable benefit to riders.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3921360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No organization can survive with a mercenary workforce, complacent culture, parasitic factions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3927360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and toothless oversight. No business in the world could ever last when labor costs outpace  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3932400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both revenue and funding. And no worker can excel without pressure, accountability, and competition.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3938560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Necessity is the mother of innovation.  Scarcity is the foundation of efficiency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3943520,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and consequences are the catalyst of urgency. There's nothing in European or Asian DNA that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3949280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "makes them inherently better at public transit. All of these countries are poorer than the United  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3954160,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "States. The difference is ultimately cultural. Countries outside the US operate with a shared  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3960000,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "social contract and collective understanding that public transit is for the public good and everyone  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3965840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must play their part to make it sustainable. Riders pay their fairs. Workers don't game the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3971200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system for personal enrichment. Unions like the workers are vested in the agency's long erm health  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3977040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the agency itself responsibly spends money to improve the overall system. But the US is a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3983280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business. Without the socialism of Europe and the collectivism of Asia, that social contract just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3988880,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't exist. Everyone comes here for money and works for money. And that mindset has carried over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3994640,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into public transit. From the CEOs who take home half a million dollars every year burning billions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3999920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in taxpayer money and the station janitors milking overtime in the storage closets to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4004720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "riders jumping the turn styles and the backroom politician chasing union votes. It's the pursuit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4009920,
    "dDurationMs": 10080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of personal immediate individual wealth that takes precedence over everything and everyone in the US."
    } ]
  } ]
}
